commit 98ee73047c63b84dbc0f34e1bd48b6911e0754e5
Author: Erik Sipsma <erik@sipsma.dev>
Date:   Fri Jun 26 14:40:53 2026 -0700

    fix(wcprof): rational root model — remove chaining inference + fallbacks
    
    Item 3, from first principles (unanimous council): the analysis must be a
    rational function of the recorded data and never compensate for it. Two pieces
    of the replay violated that and are removed:
    
      - The Run() CHAINING: it inferred a sequential dependency between successive
        or overlapping roots from their temporal order — a guess with no recorded
        causal edge (a shell serializing two CLI commands is invisible to the
        engine). Removed: every root has no incoming edge, so the data says it is
        INDEPENDENT — anchor it at its own recorded start, an exact fact. All roots
        are pre-anchored before any finish, so a cross-root wait always resolves to
        an already-anchored target.
    
      - The spawnTo recorded-offset FALLBACK for a not-yet-scheduled root: dead once
        roots are pre-anchored. The par<0 branch is now the exact root anchor
        (uncounted). The remaining corners (an op referenced from within its
        ancestor's prefix before the ancestor spawns it; a recorded child its parent
        never spawns; the joinUpTo orphan) are not approximations to choose — they
        are impossible in a faithful synchronous nesting, i.e. unfaithful DATA. They
        are flagged (FallbackAnchors, gate-failing) so the EMIT is fixed, never
        silently approximated.
    
    The counterfactual still crosses a root boundary, but only through a RECORDED
    edge: a cross-root wait propagates the saving to its waiter; an in-engine
    sub-session is a recorded nesting/launch edge (nested-client reparenting already
    does this), so it is not a pure root. The counters are now data-faithfulness
    signals: CycleWarnings + FallbackAnchors + SimStartConflicts == 0 by
    construction for faithful data; any non-zero ⇒ fix the emit.
    
    NOT bit-identical, contrary to the council's framing — and that is the win.
    Removing the chaining makes the baseline MATCH the recorded makespan, because
    the chaining was propagating each root's replay drift into later root starts:
    native 5.86s/-0.1% → 5.87s/-0.0%, OTel 5.96s/-2.4% → 6.11s/+0.0%, both now
    exact. The OTel -2.4% "drift" was entirely the chaining artifact, not an
    unrecorded wait. Multi-root what-ifs change (independent roots no longer falsely
    shift) — validated by the synthetic case-(a) (cross-root dedup: saving crosses
    the boundary, makespan 200) and case-(b) (sequential roots: scaling A does not
    shift B) fixtures, NOT by the old native ranking (the thing under suspicion).
    
    Tests: TestRootChaining → TestRootsIndependent (case b); TestCrossRootAnchor →
    TestCrossRootDedup (case a, makespan 200, 0 signals by construction);
    TestTwoZeroDurCoEnding (the co-terminating zero-dur residual); the OTel gate
    test flips (cross-root now passes with 0 fallbacks).
    
    Consequence stated honestly: cross-SESSION wall-time is now explicitly out of
    engine scope (it was being faked by the chaining). Single-query runs unaffected;
    multi-command CI timing is a separate orchestrator/multi-trace concern.
    
    Signed-off-by: Erik Sipsma <erik@sipsma.dev>

